%description:

Tests that a VLAN policy module rejects a filter VLAN id that is not an integer in its map parameter at
initialization, naming the interface and the entry. Before the check, the entry
was ignored or failed only when a packet reached it. The network is the one of
lib/vlan-access-trunk.ini, with one malformed parameter.

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib
*.bridge1.bridging.vlanPolicy.inboundFilter.acceptedVlanIds = {"eth3" : [10, "20"]}
include ../../lib/vlan-access-trunk.ini

%exitcode: 1
%postrun-command: grep '<!>' test.out test.err > vlan-map-error.out || true
%contains: vlan-map-error.out
Invalid VLAN id "20" in the acceptedVlanIds entry for interface 'eth3': expected an integer, -1 or 0 to 4094
